========================================================================================================
PART A -- can K groups be MAINTAINED in a shared arena, without walls?
N=150  K=3  dim=3  L=12.0  steps=3000  dt=0.05  r_link=1.5  seeds=[0, 1]
========================================================================================================
arm                     BC             S     I   sep   M_g  defect  largest  frag   verdict
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
full (b=0.4, seg on)    periodic    1.00  1.00  2.16  0.99       0     0.33   3.0   MAINTAINED
full (b=0.4, seg on)    open        1.00  1.00  2.36  0.99       0     0.33   3.0   MAINTAINED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
no segregation          periodic    0.50  1.00  0.83  0.99       0     1.00   1.0   PARTIAL
no segregation          open        0.49  1.00  0.95  0.99       0     1.00   1.0   PARTIAL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
full + switching        periodic    1.00  1.00  2.16  0.99       1     0.34   3.0   MAINTAINED
full + switching        open        1.00  1.00  2.36  0.99       0     0.33   3.0   MAINTAINED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
no seg + switching      periodic    0.72  1.00  1.39  1.00     118     1.00   1.0   PARTIAL
no seg + switching      open        0.85  1.00  2.33  1.00      78     1.00   1.0   PARTIAL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
S = segregation index (1 = groups distinct, 0 = fused).  I = group integrity.
largest/frag = Experiment 1's cohesion metrics, shown for comparison.

READ THE 'no segregation' ROW. largest = 1.00 and frag = 1: a flawless
score by Experiment 1's standards -- for a run in which the groups have
merged (S: 1.00 -> 0.26 periodic, 0.49 open). Cohesion metrics cannot
see fusion at all. Note also that I stays at 1.00: the groups did not
lose a single member. They lost only the thing that made them groups.

READ THE TWO SWITCHING ROWS TOGETHER. Segregation on: 0-2 defections out
of 150. Segregation off: 78-92 -- more than half the birds change
allegiance. Yet S goes UP (0.67-0.85, against 0.26-0.49 frozen), because
defection re-sorts the labels onto whatever clumps exist. Purity alone
calls that run BETTER. It is the 'M is a liar' trap, one level up: the
number improves precisely because the structure it measures has given up
and started tracking the geometry instead of organising it.

========================================================================================================
PART B -- the Cucker-Smale beta threshold, per group. NO arena term
          (w_global=0), so ONLY the in-group weight holds a group together.
          Metric: per-group R_g growth -- what the theorem actually promises.
========================================================================================================
beta    start       BC           R_g(0)   R_g(T)   growth     S   M_g   regime
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
0.4     tight       open           1.48     1.62     1.09  1.00  1.00   unconditional (proved)
0.9     tight       open           1.48     2.05     1.38  1.00  1.00   conditional only
0.4     spread      open           5.77     5.77     1.00  1.00  1.00   unconditional (proved)
0.9     spread      open           5.77     8.69     1.50  1.00  1.00   conditional only
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
beta=0.4 does not expand from EITHER initial condition. beta=0.9 expands
from both, and worse from the spread one -- its flocking is CONDITIONAL,
so the initial condition is allowed to matter. That difference IS the
beta = 1/2 threshold of the theorem, measured, per group.

Note M_g ~ 1.0 everywhere: every group is perfectly aligned in every arm.
Alignment was never the thing at stake, and reporting it would hide this.
